WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Morgan has a plausible Harbor proposal: add a free digital-skills session next month.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.700
The room note is current.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.960
The attendance note suggests interest.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.640
The facilitator is still available for review, not confirmed.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.320
A colleague suggests paying for a small printing run to test flyers.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.960
The amount sounds minor.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.100
Morgan stops at the word 'paying.'

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.200
A recommendation can sit in the brief.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.680
A purchase needs a separate human decision.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:32.780
The same paper workflow now has two questions: should Harbor propose the session, and should anyone authorize a specific expense?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:41.880
Chapter Seventeen's Spend Envelope names amount, counterparty, purpose, execution window, retry limit, trace, and approval.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.880
The workbook adds currency, requesting role, forbidden actions, and revocation.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.500
In the Harbor case, use a proposed forty-dollar print test with the course printer and a two-day window.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.460
The number is classroom arithmetic, not a quote, budget, or authorization.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.340
The envelope is incomplete until the actual approving human can see the evidence and exact terms.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.240
It cannot be stretched into a recurring charge or an 'up to' range.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.220
Harbor's preparation role has no payment authority.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:19.100
It may draft a spend request; it cannot place an order, enter a card, increase a cap, or trigger paid API usage.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.540
Put a closed gate between the proposed envelope and any dollar-moving verb.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:29.380
If the cost, vendor, window, or evidence changes, the paper envelope goes back to Morgan.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.920
If it expires, it stays closed.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.820
A prior approval of the session idea would not approve the print order.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.300
The approval has to match the action.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.900
Now write the decision Morgan actually owns.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:49.740
Chapter Eighteen uses five sections: context, options, recommendation, reversibility, and what would change our mind.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.480
Option A is to propose a session subject to facilitator confirmation.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.320
Option B is to hold the proposal and gather a fresh staffing commitment.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.700
Give B a fair case: it protects Harbor from promising a session it cannot staff.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:09.300
The recommendation can favor A only if the brief clearly carries that condition.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.160
Morgan can also choose hold.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.960
The agent's framing must leave room for disagreement.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.320
Put the spend question on its own line.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.200
Even if Morgan favors a conditional session proposal, the print request remains held.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:27.280
The brief should name Morgan as decision owner, the course deadline, the evidence gap, and what can be reversed.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.260
A draft brief can be withdrawn.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.400
A flyer sent into the community cannot be pulled back with the same ease.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:37.740
That difference is why preparation and side effects have different gates.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:44.720
An honest decision brief makes the strongest alternative visible and tells the reviewer what evidence would overturn the recommendation.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:45.820
Pause.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:50.420
Which sentence in the brief would stop 'available for review' from becoming 'confirmed'?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.200
Fill a Spend Envelope, then a Decision Brief.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:05.000
Give the envelope an exact illustrative amount, named course counterparty, purpose, window, one-or-zero retry limit, trace, human approver, and revocation condition.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.300
Mark it unapproved.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:15.300
Give the brief two real options, a fair case for the rejected option, a recommendation, reversibility, evidence gap, and a hold outcome.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.460
Keep the facilitator unconfirmed.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.780
Use a fictional or approved example.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:27.120
Do not use private operational data, open a checkout, use a card, call a provider, or publish a session.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:14.340
Save revision ten as a draft.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.920
Morgan has two distinct decisions and the evidence for both.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:19.640
Neither has been exercised.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:26.020
Next we will make the pending work visible without turning a phone notification into a second control room.
